sequenceDiagram
  %% Evidence: backend/src/routes/auth.rs, services/password.rs, services/jwt.rs, services/sessions.rs, services/mfa_accounts.rs, services/mfa_challenges.rs
  actor User
  participant Browser
  participant Auth as Auth routes
  participant Security as Password and MFA services
  participant Redis
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant JWT as JWT service

  alt Register or password-only login
    User->>Browser: Submit credentials
    Browser->>Auth: Register or login request
    Auth->>Security: Validate and verify or hash password
    Auth->>DB: Load or create active identity
    alt MFA enabled
      Auth->>Redis: Store hash-keyed pre-authentication record
      Auth-->>Browser: MFA required without a session
      User->>Browser: Enter TOTP or recovery proof
      Browser->>Auth: Complete MFA challenge
      Auth->>Redis: Lock and consume pre-authentication record
      Auth->>DB: Verify replay-safe MFA state
      Auth->>JWT: Issue AAL2 access and refresh credentials
    else MFA not enabled
      Auth->>JWT: Issue AAL1 access and refresh credentials
    end
    Auth->>DB: Store logical session and refresh-token hash
    Auth-->>Browser: Access token and HttpOnly refresh cookie
  else Refresh
    Browser->>Auth: Refresh with HttpOnly cookie and Origin
    Auth->>DB: Lock family and validate AAL and AMR context
    Auth->>DB: Rotate and link successor transactionally
    Auth->>JWT: Preserve assurance context in new access token
    Auth-->>Browser: Access token and rotated HttpOnly cookie
  end

  Note over Browser,Auth: Public password reset, email verification, passkeys, and administrative MFA recovery remain deferred
